{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":44634,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"10cb7da3ba3259ab19074b8b06122dc6","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; I&#039;ve been busy for a few weeks and havent been able to see whats been going on and wow I&#039;ve missed a lot. Reading it all over I&#039;m starting to kinda panic because guests are starting to ask how the day is going to go and I have no idea! JMarie thanks so much for the inof and the pics are beautiful...do you know if they always do the cake\/dances bouqet right after? I don&#039;t care the order but some of the guests are kind of antsy to know whats going on and I have no answers for them!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1250398,"PostDate":1281557082,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> I've been busy for a few weeks and havent been able to see whats been going on and wow I've missed a lot. Reading it all over I'm starting to kinda panic because guests are starting to ask how the day is going to go and I have no idea! JMarie thanks so much for the inof and the pics are beautiful...do you know if they always do the cake\/dances bouqet right after? I don't care the order but some of the guests are kind of antsy to know whats going on and I have no answers for them!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;46;23\/st\/20110111\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/16e1\/event.png\">http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt...16e1\/event.png<\/a><\/div><\/div>","Email":"sara.willy@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1259221185,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-223542.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":100,"PhotoHeight":75,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"soontobemrsdow","Id":223542,"Name":"soontobemrsdow","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":44634,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"01bf5402752a3fe0a0a467af0cbef111","RawContent":"Thanks for the information JMarie! That&#039;s awesome. I can&#039;t see the pics yet but maybe once I get enough posts? I like the idea of the piano bar too - way cheaper. And I&#039;m glad to hear everyone loved the food at Dolce Vita.","Attachments":[],"Id":1250428,"PostDate":1281557815,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Thanks for the information JMarie! That's awesome. I can't see the pics yet but maybe once I get enough posts? I like the idea of the piano bar too - way cheaper. And I'm glad to hear everyone loved the food at Dolce Vita.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><span>Getting married in Runaway Bay, Jamaica February 2011!!!<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"ashleyl_84@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1271190989,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-227291.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"AshleyL","Id":227291,"Name":"AshleyL","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":44634,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"668979d8a40f966aa54ab466c34638e9","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; those pics are amazing...I get more and more excited to finally get down there everytime I am on this site. Thanks so much for sharing info and pics with all of us. Looks like I have to get a portable steamemer, I am thinking they are only around $50.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;  &lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; We arent having an AHR so Ill be wearing my dress all day, I think I might be one of the only one&#039;s though.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1250431,"PostDate":1281557907,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> those pics are amazing...I get more and more excited to finally get down there everytime I am on this site. Thanks so much for sharing info and pics with all of us. Looks like I have to get a portable steamemer, I am thinking they are only around $50.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> We arent having an AHR so Ill be wearing my dress all day, I think I might be one of the only one's though.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><span>Today I marry my bestfriend, the one I laugh with, the one I love.<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"kfairful@alumni.uoguelph.ca","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1272162450,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-227617.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":267,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"katelynn","Id":227617,"Name":"katelynn","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":44634,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f14476b076f09f90af7c25e50f980681","RawContent":"\n\n&lt;div class=\"quote-container\"&gt;&lt;span&gt;Quote:&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;div class=\"quote-block\"&gt;Originally Posted by &lt;strong&gt;akua420&lt;\/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;img style=\"border: 0px solid;\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" class=\"inlineimg\" alt=\"View Post\"\/&gt;\n\n&lt;p&gt;\n Thats what I&#039;m planning on doing too.&amp;nbsp; My mom just went to Mexico and there was a bride on the plane and the flight attendant put it in the very front area and hung it up so it didn&#039;t get wrinkled.&amp;nbsp; Thats my plan, I hopefully won&#039;t have to do anythign whe nI&#039;m down.&amp;nbsp; The nice thing abuot the material in the dress though is its gathered, and you can&#039;t really see the wrinkles when its on, thank goodness.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;\n\n\n \n That would be awesome if they let you store it up front. In our travel package it just says Bride and Groom get priority seating on the plane so they can store dress\/tux in overhead compartment. Hopefully I can find something better than cramming it up there.","Attachments":[],"Id":1250432,"PostDate":1281557991,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <br><br><div class=\"quote-container\"><span>Quote:<\/span><div class=\"quote-block\">Originally Posted by <strong>akua420<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' style=\"border: 0px solid;\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" class=\"inlineimg\" alt=\"View Post\"\/><\/span><br><br><p><br> Thats what I'm planning on doing too.\u00a0 My mom just went to Mexico and there was a bride on the plane and the flight attendant put it in the very front area and hung it up so it didn't get wrinkled.\u00a0 Thats my plan, I hopefully won't have to do anythign whe nI'm down.\u00a0 The nice thing abuot the material in the dress though is its gathered, and you can't really see the wrinkles when its on, thank goodness.\u00a0<\/p><\/div><\/div><br><br><br> <br> That would be awesome if they let you store it up front. In our travel package it just says Bride and Groom get priority seating on the plane so they can store dress\/tux in overhead compartment. Hopefully I can find something better than cramming it up there.\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><span>Getting married in Runaway Bay, Jamaica February 2011!!!<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"ashleyl_84@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1271190989,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-227291.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"AshleyL","Id":227291,"Name":"AshleyL","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":44634,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"84bd38127cc1ed4ab2f1b32d83169729","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; missy&amp;amp;eric2011- haha thats so funny!&amp;nbsp; Actually I&#039;ve been on vacation visiting fam and&amp;nbsp;we had a&amp;nbsp;friends wedding to go to&amp;nbsp;and work has been crazy so haven&#039;t had a chance to log on in a while...it was killing me! lol.&amp;nbsp; I&#039;ve been working awful hours this week and next and it sucks bc I want to get my save the dates out..grr!&amp;nbsp; Hopefully I can work on them on Sunday!&amp;nbsp; Love the music picks btw, those are great!!&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;  &lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; JMarie, thanks so much for your review and the pics!!! It looks like your wedding was beautiful and I love your dress! Congrats! :)&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;  &lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Beverly told me that you can bring in outside venders at no additional cost so you can use a different florist if you want.&amp;nbsp; I think if you go to the tai flora (or whatever its called) website, they have examples of bouquets that I&#039;m assuming are similar to what we get to choose from.&amp;nbsp; I&#039;m not a big fan of fake flowers, but I also don&#039;t really want to dish out a bunch of money on the guys bouts since none of them care anyway, so is anyone using something other than flowers?&amp;nbsp; I&#039;ve seen girls use feathers or shells...so I was just wondering if anyone had any good ideas.&amp;nbsp; As for centerpieces, I&#039;m not sure what to do.&amp;nbsp; I originally wanted to do the floating candles\/ orchids in vases of water but like some of you said before, I am stressing over the thought of bringing down vases...what a pain!&amp;nbsp; So I&#039;m tossing around the idea of using pictures of use instead.&amp;nbsp; Pics of when we were little all the way up to now and put them in pretty matching frames, having them on the tables and surrounding the frames with shells or stones, petals...something like that.&amp;nbsp; And then adding some candles around as well.&amp;nbsp; But idk, we have plenty of time to figure it out but thats just an idea that I was thinking about.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;  &lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Anyway, my laptop is dying so got to go!&amp;nbsp; Great to see everyone so involved on this thread!!!! :)&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1250433,"PostDate":1281557994,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> missy&eric2011- haha thats so funny!\u00a0 Actually I've been on vacation visiting fam and\u00a0we had a\u00a0friends wedding to go to\u00a0and work has been crazy so haven't had a chance to log on in a while...it was killing me! lol.\u00a0 I've been working awful hours this week and next and it sucks bc I want to get my save the dates out..grr!\u00a0 Hopefully I can work on them on Sunday!\u00a0 Love the music picks btw, those are great!!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> JMarie, thanks so much for your review and the pics!!! It looks like your wedding was beautiful and I love your dress! Congrats! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Beverly told me that you can bring in outside venders at no additional cost so you can use a different florist if you want.\u00a0 I think if you go to the tai flora (or whatever its called) website, they have examples of bouquets that I'm assuming are similar to what we get to choose from.\u00a0 I'm not a big fan of fake flowers, but I also don't really want to dish out a bunch of money on the guys bouts since none of them care anyway, so is anyone using something other than flowers?\u00a0 I've seen girls use feathers or shells...so I was just wondering if anyone had any good ideas.\u00a0 As for centerpieces, I'm not sure what to do.\u00a0 I originally wanted to do the floating candles\/ orchids in vases of water but like some of you said before, I am stressing over the thought of bringing down vases...what a pain!\u00a0 So I'm tossing around the idea of using pictures of use instead.\u00a0 Pics of when we were little all the way up to now and put them in pretty matching frames, having them on the tables and surrounding the frames with shells or stones, petals...something like that.\u00a0 And then adding some candles around as well.\u00a0 But idk, we have plenty of time to figure it out but thats just an idea that I was thinking about.\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Anyway, my laptop is dying so got to go!\u00a0 Great to see everyone so involved on this thread!!!! <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mekanabr@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1259797911,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-223677.JPG?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":299,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"mekanabr","Id":223677,"Name":"mekanabr","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":44634,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"b097fee74d7e4293c9aa028e91507caf","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]soontobemrsdow[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n I&#039;ve been busy for a few weeks and havent been able to see whats been going on and wow I&#039;ve missed a lot. Reading it all over I&#039;m starting to kinda panic because guests are starting to ask how the day is going to go and I have no idea! JMarie thanks so much for the inof and the pics are beautiful...do you know if they always do the cake\/dances bouqet right after? I don&#039;t care the order but some of the guests are kind of antsy to know whats going on and I have no answers for them![\/quote] \n \n Just saw your post... tell your guests to RELAX.  lol, I mean as long as they know to show up at xx time for the ceremony, why does it really matter what order everything is happening in, were they planning to do something else that day? [img]http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheesy.gif[\/img]   Just tell them the ceremony is at xx time and dinner is at (most likely) 6:30...No need for you to panic over it!!!!","Attachments":[],"Id":1250454,"PostDate":1281558350,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <br \/> <br \/> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>soontobemrsdow<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" style=\"border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> I've been busy for a few weeks and havent been able to see whats been going on and wow I've missed a lot. Reading it all over I'm starting to kinda panic because guests are starting to ask how the day is going to go and I have no idea! JMarie thanks so much for the inof and the pics are beautiful...do you know if they always do the cake\/dances bouqet right after? I don't care the order but some of the guests are kind of antsy to know whats going on and I have no answers for them!<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> <br \/> Just saw your post... tell your guests to RELAX.\u00a0 lol, I mean as long as they know to show up at xx time for the ceremony, why does it really matter what order everything is happening in, were they planning to do something else that day? <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"\" height=\"16\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/cheesy.gif\" title=\"\" width=\"16\" \/><\/span>\u00a0\u00a0 Just tell them the ceremony is at xx time and dinner is at (most likely) 6:30...No need for you to panic over it!!!!\u00a0<br \/> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mekanabr@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1259797911,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-223677.JPG?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":299,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"mekanabr","Id":223677,"Name":"mekanabr","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":44634,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"c47419ba62205709882a81f88c2f461f","RawContent":"[quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]mekanabr[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n   \n Beverly told me that you can bring in outside venders at no additional cost so you can use a different florist if you want.  I think if you go to the tai flora (or whatever its called) website, they have examples of bouquets that I&#039;m assuming are similar to what we get to choose from.  I&#039;m not a big fan of fake flowers, but I also don&#039;t really want to dish out a bunch of money on the guys bouts since none of them care anyway, so is anyone using something other than flowers?  I&#039;ve seen girls use feathers or shells...so I was just wondering if anyone had any good ideas.  As for centerpieces, I&#039;m not sure what to do.  I originally wanted to do the floating candles\/ orchids in vases of water but like some of you said before, I am stressing over the thought of bringing down vases...what a pain!  So I&#039;m tossing around the idea of using pictures of use instead.  Pics of when we were little all the way up to now and put them in pretty matching frames, having them on the tables and surrounding the frames with shells or stones, petals...something like that.  And then adding some candles around as well.  But idk, we have plenty of time to figure it out but thats just an idea that I was thinking about.  \n   \n  [\/quote] \n \n \n I haven&#039;t even thought about bringing down decorations!  Are you bringing down a cake topper too?!  I already planned to bring down the jars for the sand ceremony...geez...I am going to end up bringing everything but the kitchen sink!!!! \n   \n I have read other comments from ladies on the site that Tia is Waaaay more expensive than the other vendors in the area.  My quote was originally for $3000 and I thought that was ridiculous; not to mention they were very unfriendly to deal with!  But I think that price is even worse when it&#039;s impossible to take them home and enjoy them after the wedding!  I think I am going to do some checking and see who else is in that area as a vendor.  \n   \n sorry...I sound negative...Refresh....Wedding...In Jamaica....Okay...I&#039;m better!  [img]http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/smile43.gif[\/img]","Attachments":[],"Id":1250487,"PostDate":1281559171,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <br \/> <br \/> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>mekanabr<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" style=\"border-bottom: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-right: 0px solid\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Beverly told me that you can bring in outside venders at no additional cost so you can use a different florist if you want.\u00a0 I think if you go to the tai flora (or whatever its called) website, they have examples of bouquets that I'm assuming are similar to what we get to choose from.\u00a0 I'm not a big fan of fake flowers, but I also don't really want to dish out a bunch of money on the guys bouts since none of them care anyway, so is anyone using something other than flowers?\u00a0 I've seen girls use feathers or shells...so I was just wondering if anyone had any good ideas.\u00a0 As for centerpieces, I'm not sure what to do.\u00a0 I originally wanted to do the floating candles\/ orchids in vases of water but like some of you said before, I am stressing over the thought of bringing down vases...what a pain!\u00a0 So I'm tossing around the idea of using pictures of use instead.\u00a0 Pics of when we were little all the way up to now and put them in pretty matching frames, having them on the tables and surrounding the frames with shells or stones, petals...something like that.\u00a0 And then adding some candles around as well.\u00a0 But idk, we have plenty of time to figure it out but thats just an idea that I was thinking about.\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> <br \/> <br \/> I haven't even thought about bringing down decorations!\u00a0 Are you bringing down a cake topper too?!\u00a0 I already planned to bring down the jars for the sand ceremony...geez...I am going to end up bringing everything but the kitchen sink!!!!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I have read other comments from ladies on the site that Tia is Waaaay more expensive than the other vendors in the area.\u00a0 My quote was originally for $3000 and I thought that was ridiculous; not to mention they were very unfriendly to deal with!\u00a0 But I think that price is\u00a0even worse\u00a0when it's impossible to take them home and enjoy them after the wedding!\u00a0 I think I am going to do some checking and see who else is in that area as a vendor.\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> sorry...I sound negative...Refresh....Wedding...In Jamaica....Okay...I'm better!\u00a0 <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"\" height=\"44\" src=\"http:\/\/files.bestdestinationwedding.com\/images\/smilies\/smile43.gif\" title=\"\" width=\"66\" \/><\/span><\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"melissa.bowen@state.mn.us","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1277427137,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-229519.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":160,"PhotoHeight":120,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"missy&eric2011","Id":229519,"Name":"missy&eric2011","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":44634,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"cd8dcc681afa18e2d7f67d1b28ffb113","RawContent":"The piano bar does sound really cute1  Great idea!\n \n   [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]missy&amp;amp;eric2011[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n JMarie - What nights is the piano bar available?  Do they play every night?  I know All of us on here are getting married on different nights...Do you remember what is available?  \n   \n Okay ladies, after her review, I am really up in the air as to what we are going to do...I was totally set on the gazebo idea...but now I am questioning it if it is that much fun doing the \"included\" stuff!!!  \n   \n I am bringing down a small handheld steamer to \"freshen\" up my dress...but hopefully I won&#039;t have to worry about wrinkles too much.  I am bringing down 2 dresses as I don&#039;t want to have to dry clean my \"real\" dress before my AHR...I am changing into the other dress sometime after the ceremony (don&#039;t know if I will wait until after dinner or not) and I am also wearing this same dress for the TTD session...anyone else doing something like this???[\/quote] \n \n \n I&#039;m contemplating doing the two dresses thing too.  There is an adorable white dress at BCBG that is CALLING ME NAME every day when I walk past at lunch. but my mom keeps insisting that I will want to wear the dress all day, but it seems like that would be HOT!  And I don&#039;t want to have to clean it.  So we will see.  What does your second dress look like?","Attachments":[],"Id":1250520,"PostDate":1281560186,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> The piano bar does sound really cute1\u00a0 Great idea!<br \/> <br \/> \u00a0<\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>missy&eric2011<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" style=\"border-right: 0px solid; border-top: 0px solid; border-left: 0px solid; border-bottom: 0px solid\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> JMarie - What nights is the piano bar available?\u00a0 Do they play every night?\u00a0 I know All of us on here are getting married on different nights...Do you remember what is available?\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Okay ladies, after her review, I am really up in the air as to what we are going to do...I was totally set on the gazebo idea...but now I am questioning it if it is that much fun doing the \"included\" stuff!!!\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I am bringing down a small handheld steamer to \"freshen\" up my dress...but hopefully I won't have to worry about wrinkles too much.\u00a0 I am bringing down 2 dresses as I don't want to have to\u00a0dry clean my \"real\" dress\u00a0before my AHR...I am changing into the other dress sometime after\u00a0the ceremony (don't know if\u00a0I will wait until after dinner or not) and I am also wearing this same dress for the TTD session...anyone else doing something like this???<\/p> <\/blockquote> <p> <br \/> <br \/> I'm contemplating doing the two dresses thing too.\u00a0 There is an adorable white dress at BCBG that is CALLING ME NAME every day when I walk past at lunch. but my mom keeps insisting that I will want to wear the dress all day, but it seems like that would be HOT!\u00a0 And I don't want to have to clean it.\u00a0 So we will see.\u00a0 What does your second dress look like?\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><span>Gran Bahia Principe - Runaway Bay - February 22, 2011<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"akua420@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1270637423,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-227119.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":161,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"akua420","Id":227119,"Name":"akua420","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":44634,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"82c670c28ce3dff7c6ea8725f082f4f2","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; \n  &lt;\/p&gt; &lt;div class=\"quote-container\"&gt; &lt;div class=\"quote-block\"&gt; &lt;p&gt; \n \n I&#039;m contemplating doing the two dresses thing too.&amp;nbsp; There is an adorable white dress at BCBG that is CALLING ME NAME every day when I walk past at lunch. but my mom keeps insisting that I will want to wear the dress all day, but it seems like that would be HOT!&amp;nbsp; And I don&#039;t want to have to clean it.&amp;nbsp; So we will see.&amp;nbsp; What does your second dress look like?&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;\/div&gt; &lt;\/div&gt; &lt;p&gt; \n \n My \"real\" dress is the Jenna by Maggie Sottero...tons of layers and would cost another fortune to have it dry cleaned...hence the second dress...&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt;  &lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; My TTD dress\/second dress is still a bridal gown... Mori lee 2203...I bought it off the rack as a sample for only $200...so i cant complain; plus I dont have to have it altered at all...its a bit long&amp;nbsp;but that&amp;nbsp;isn&#039;t a big deal.&amp;nbsp; I still wanted to look and feel like a bride but I didnt want it to look anything like my real dress as my FI helped with picking this one out and originally we were thinking about doing the TTD pics the day before the wedding being as our wedding package comes with a trial hairdo...but then i saw the after affects of the sand with the dresses and decided that the day after the ceremony would be the best if i wanted any nice pictures in the second dress.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1250547,"PostDate":1281560761,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> <br \/> \u00a0<\/p> <div class=\"quote-container\"> <div class=\"quote-block\"> <p> <br \/> <br \/> I'm contemplating doing the two dresses thing too.\u00a0 There is an adorable white dress at BCBG that is CALLING ME NAME every day when I walk past at lunch. but my mom keeps insisting that I will want to wear the dress all day, but it seems like that would be HOT!\u00a0 And I don't want to have to clean it.\u00a0 So we will see.\u00a0 What does your second dress look like?\u00a0<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <\/div> <\/div> <p> <br \/> <br \/> My \"real\" dress is the Jenna by Maggie Sottero...tons of layers and would cost another fortune to have it dry cleaned...hence the second dress...<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> My TTD dress\/second dress is still a bridal gown... Mori lee 2203...I bought it off the rack as a sample for only $200...so i cant complain; plus I dont have to have it altered at all...its a bit long\u00a0but that\u00a0isn't a big deal.\u00a0 I still wanted to look and feel like a bride but I didnt want it to look anything like my real dress as my FI helped with picking this one out and originally we were thinking about doing the TTD pics the day before the wedding being as our wedding package comes with a trial hairdo...but then i saw the after affects of the sand with the dresses and decided that the day after the ceremony would be the best if i wanted any nice pictures in the second dress.\u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"melissa.bowen@state.mn.us","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1277427137,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-229519.gif?_r=0","PhotoWidth":160,"PhotoHeight":120,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"missy&eric2011","Id":229519,"Name":"missy&eric2011","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":44634,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"f9c9ff7855621bb0779100632a95fb8d","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; So I finally got to 150 and it STILL won&#039;t let me access pics.&amp;nbsp; Maybe you have to be at 151?   I will post this and try.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1250600,"PostDate":1281561748,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> So I finally got to 150 and it STILL won't let me access pics.\u00a0 Maybe you have to be at 151?\u00a0\u00a0 I will post this and try.<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div class=\"post-sig post-sig-limit shazam usersig-click\"><div class=\"reparse-sig-lineheight\"><span>Gran Bahia Principe - Runaway Bay - February 22, 2011<\/span><\/div><\/div>","Email":"akua420@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1270637423,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-227119.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":161,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"akua420","Id":227119,"Name":"akua420","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":5564,"TotalPages":557,"CurrentPage":240,"NextPage":250,"PreviousPage":230,"LastPage":5560},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
